+# Performance report: BlockInfo (block counts panel and hover highlight)
+
+**Workload**: a build with about 6,000 placed blocks. Client MicroProfiler capture on desktop, plus
+frame rate on a phone (numbers from the user). The "After" column has not been measured yet: that
+is the first item under "For you to verify".
+
+**Bottleneck**: script time on the client. `Script_BlockInfo` took about 2.5 ms every frame, and
+most frames had a GC label right after it. An empty baseplate was fine on both devices, so the
+cost grows with the block count.
+
+`src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/BlockInfo.client.luau` did all of this inside
+`RenderStepped`, every frame:
+
+1. `blocksFolder:GetChildren()` three times: once for the per-type counts, once for the hover
+   search, once for the total. Each call builds a new 6,000-entry array (about 48 KB each, about
+   150 KB of garbage per frame, roughly 9 MB per second at 60 FPS). That garbage is what the GC
+   label after the script was collecting.
+2. 6,000 `block.Name` reads for the counts, then 6,000 `IsA` calls and 6,000 `Position` reads
+   to find the hovered block. Each engine read costs about 50 to 100 ns, so these alone come to
+   roughly 1 to 2 ms per frame at 6,000 blocks, and they grow in step with the build.
+3. Rebuilt the label text by appending to a string in a loop and wrote it to `Text`, even when
+   nothing had changed.
+
+Everything except the raycast scaled with the block count, so 12,000 blocks would have cost about
+twice as much, and phones pay several times what a desktop does.
+
+| Metric (6,000 blocks) | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Script_BlockInfo` per frame, desktop | about 2.5 ms | not measured yet (expected well under 0.1 ms) |
+| GC label after the script | most frames | not measured yet (expected gone) |
+| Phone FPS | about 35 | not measured yet |
+| Per-frame work that grows with block count | 3 `GetChildren`, about 18,000 engine reads | none |
+
+**Changes**, highest level first:
+
+- **Counts follow events instead of being recounted.** The script counts the existing children
+  once at startup, then updates the per-type counts and the total from `ChildAdded` and
+  `ChildRemoved`. A block costs work once when it is placed or removed, not on every frame.
+- **The hover search asks the engine for nearby blocks only.** After the same mouse raycast, a
+  `GetPartBoundsInRadius` query (radius = one block size, filtered to the Blocks folder) returns
+  the handful of blocks near the hit point, and the script picks the nearest center within the
+  radius, as before. The query's cost depends on how many parts sit in that small sphere, not on
+  the size of the build.
+- **The label is rebuilt only when it would change**: when a count changes or the hovered block
+  changes. The text is built with `table.concat`. On a frame where nothing changed the script does
+  one raycast, one small query, and stops.
+- `RaycastParams` and `OverlapParams` are created once and reused. The character filter is
+  updated only when the character changes.
+
+**Behavior**: unchanged for players. Same panel, same lines in the same order, same "Total"
+(it still counts every child of the Blocks folder), same "Pointing at" line, same selection box
+and hover radius. The differences, none reachable with the current code:
+
+- A block renamed after it is placed would keep being counted under its old name. The server
+  never renames blocks.
+- Parts with `CanQuery` off are invisible to the hover query. The server never turns it off.
+- When two blocks are exactly the same distance from the hit point, the old code picked the one
+  that came first in the folder; the new code may pick the other. This needs a float-exact tie on
+  a raycast hit and would change at most which of two equally close blocks is outlined.
+- With deferred signals on, a newly placed or removed block shows in the counts at the end of the
+  frame it arrives in, which nobody can see.
+
+**Tried and reverted**: nothing.
+
+**Left alone**:
+
+- The raycast itself runs every frame. It is a few microseconds, and the mouse and camera move
+  most frames, so skipping it when they are still would save almost nothing.
+- A Luau grid index for the hover search would be faster than the engine query, but one query
+  per frame costs a couple of microseconds, and the engine query also stays correct if blocks
+  ever move or stop snapping to the grid.
+- The panel's ScreenGui holds only this panel, so a text change redraws nothing else.
+
+**For you to verify**:
+
+1. **Studio, desktop.** In the same 6,000-block build, take a client MicroProfiler capture
+   (Ctrl+F6, then pause and look at a few frames). `Script_BlockInfo` should drop from about
+   2.5 ms to a few hundredths of a millisecond, and the GC label after it should be gone or rare.
+   Fill in the "After" column.
+2. **Scaling.** Repeat at about twice the block count (12,000 or more). `Script_BlockInfo` should
+   stay about the same. If it grows with the build, something still scales and I want to see the
+   capture.
+3. **Behavior.** Check by hand, since no spec covers this script:
+   - The counts and total match the build at join, after placing blocks of each type, and after
+     blocks are removed (if your game removes blocks, or by deleting some in the server view).
+   - Hovering a block outlines it and shows "Pointing at: <type>". Pointing at the baseplate right
+     next to a block still outlines that block (within one block size), as before.
+   - Moving off all blocks, or pointing at the sky, clears the outline and the "Pointing at" line.
+   - After respawning, your own character still does not block the hover ray.
+4. **Phone.** Publish and check FPS on the same phone in the same build. Studio cannot show
+   phone frame rate. Other costs may now show up there (for example rendering thousands of
+   parts), which would be the next thing to profile.
+
+I could not run StyLua or selene on the changed script in this session, because the command
+needed approval and none was available. Run `stylua` and `selene` on
+`src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/BlockInfo.client.luau` before committing.
